1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,033
Same Minnesota home, same winter.

2
00:00:02,153 --> 00:00:05,740
One heats with electric baseboards, the other with a heat pump.

3
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:10,934
The baseboard home pays about two thousand three hundred forty-two dollars a year for heat.

4
00:00:11,054 --> 00:00:14,262
The heat pump home pays about one thousand sixty-five.

5
00:00:14,382 --> 00:00:19,013
Why? A baseboard turns one unit of electricity into one unit of heat.

6
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:25,062
A heat pump moves heat from outside, about two point two units for every unit of electricity.

7
00:00:25,182 --> 00:00:33,876
Even zero-degree air still holds about eighty-seven percent of the heat energy of seventy-degree air, counted from absolute zero.

8
00:00:33,996 --> 00:00:38,261
That's about one thousand two hundred seventy-six dollars saved every year.

9
00:00:38,381 --> 00:00:39,816
Same home, same winter…
